    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70-a1">

                <pb facs="0186" n="80" xml:id="pg80"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 58.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pacheco to Señor Galindo</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States in Guatemala and
                                Honduras</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-08-30"><hi rendition="#italic">August 30,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor of communicating to your excellency that steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">City of Panama</hi> will make regular trip to your
                    ports, and my Government desires assurance that the steamer will not be detained
                    over usual limit as per contract, and expects that time will he had for full
                    inquiry into this affair, giving at same time assurance that due respect shall
                    be shown to the sovereignty of your excellency’s Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. Pacheco</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
